# Supply-chain safety: refuse to resolve any package version published within the
# last 7 days. Freshly-published versions are the window in which a compromised
# maintainer account or a malicious release is most likely to still be live, so we
# let the ecosystem look at a release before we pull it in.
#
# Bun is this project's package manager (see CLAUDE.md) and bunfig.toml carries
# the authoritative setting. This file only exists so the same policy applies if
# someone reaches for npm; there is deliberately no package-lock.json, since a
# second lockfile would make Vercel and CI disagree about which manager to use.
#
# npm spells this in DAYS; bun spells it in seconds. Keep the two in sync.
# Requires npm >= 11.6.1; older npm ignores it silently.
min-release-age=7
